      "description": {
        "fun": "A bundle of energy that can't sit still: Scorbunny warms up with a run until fire energy courses through its body and the pads on its feet and nose blaze with heat. Hot enough to start small fires, those footpads hit hard when it kicks. The yellow mark across its nose comes from a Japanese character trope, a plaster on the nose that marks a rambunctious kid.",
        "guide": "The Fire-type first partner Pokémon of Galar, from Pokémon Sword and Shield. Scorbunny runs to warm up, sending fire energy to pads on its feet and nose that grow hot enough to burn. It evolves into Raboot and then Cinderace.",
        "tagline": "A sprinting bunny whose feet heat up for fiery kicks",
